    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: D(n)=round(n!/e) proved on optimal domain n≥1 (sharpening sibling oq-03 n≥2), plus sharpness at n=0. Docker-verified 0 sorry/0 axiom, PR #35007.",
    "builtItems": [
      "round_eq_of_abs_sub_lt_half in DerangementsConvergenceOQ02OQ01.lean:55 — generic rounding criterion",
      "exp_neg_one_lt_half:64 — e⁻¹<1/2 from Real.add_one_lt_exp",
      "abs_numDerangements_sub_lt_half:75 — strict |D(n)-n!·e⁻¹|<1/2 for n≥1",
      "numDerangements_eq_round:118 — D(n)=round(n!/e) for n≥1 (extends oq-03 n≥2)",
      "numDerangements_eq_floor:126 — floor form D(n)=⌊n!·e⁻¹+1/2⌋",
      "round_factorial_exp_zero:135 / numDerangements_round_ne_at_zero:145 — sharpness at n=0"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "The folklore identity D(n)=round(n!/e) is FALSE at n=0: round(0!·e⁻¹)=round(e⁻¹)=0 but D(0)=1. The correct universal statement starts at n=1.",
      "The exact threshold n≥1 (vs the sibling oq-03 n≥2) hinges on a single analytic fact: at n=1 the rate bound |D(n)/n!-e⁻¹|≤1/(n+1)! scales to a NON-strict ≤1/2, so strictness needs e⁻¹<1/2 (i.e. e>2) supplied separately.",
      "Isolating |x-m|<1/2 ⟹ round x=m as a reusable lemma (round_eq_of_abs_sub_lt_half, via round_eq + Int.floor_eq_iff + linarith) serves BOTH the positive identity (m=D(n)) and the negative sharpness fact (m=0)."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Formalize the exact rounding margin asymptotics: |D(n)-n!/e| < 1/(n+1) and ~1/(n+1); find the n where n!/e is closest to a half-integer (worst case for rounding).",
      "Investigate nearest-integer characterizations of other e-adjacent sequences (involutions, ⌊n!·e^c⌉) and how their optimal threshold depends on c."
    ],
